# Method 2 ÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ Frequency Count Array (Best for Lowercase English Letters)

## Idea

Count character frequencies.

* increment for first string
* decrement for second string

If all counts become zero ÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ anagram.

---

## Code

```java id="yl5w1o"
public class AnagramCheck {

    public static boolean isAnagram(String s1, String s2) {

        s1 = s1.toLowerCase();
        s2 = s2.toLowerCase();

        if (s1.length() != s2.length()) {
            return false;
        }

        int[] freq = new int[26];

        for (int i = 0; i < s1.length(); i++) {
            freq[s1.charAt(i) - 'a']++;
            freq[s2.charAt(i) - 'a']--;
        }

        for (int count : freq) {
            if (count != 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(isAnagram("listen", "silent"));
    }
}
```

---

# Why `char - 'a'` Works

ASCII values:

'a'=97,;'b'=98,;'c'=99

Example:

```java id="v9qqd0"
'c' - 'a'
= 99 - 97
= 2
```

So:

* `'a'` ÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ index 0
* `'b'` ÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ index 1
* `'c'` ÃÂ¢ÃÂÃÂ index 2

---

## Complexity

Traversal only:

O(n)

Most efficient approach for lowercase alphabets.

